      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>The mission of the Center is to promote and preserve Serbian language and heritage and to introduce Serbian traditions and customs to the multicultural community.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>During the year, the Serbian Cultural Center continued to fulfill its mission of preserving and promoting Serbian language, culture, and heritage in the local community. The Center successfully operated the School of Serbian Language and Culture, serving 55 students in classroom and 21 students online. Classes were held weekly on Saturdays from 2:25 p.m. to 4:45 p.m. In addition, the Center hosted the Nikola Tesla Club, with 30 students actively participating. The Club organized 10 workshops and one educational trip to New York City, where children performed a play about Nikola Tesla and received awards for their talents at an international Tesla conference.The Center also maintained an active Drama club, engaging 20 children in theater and stage performances that foster both language learning and cultural awareness.Throughout the year, the organization organized Annual Fundraising Gala Dinner, December Nights at Balboa park, a movie screening and several smaller cultural gatherings to strengthen community ties and promote intercultural understanding. These events brought together members and friends of the community, celebrating Serbian traditions while building connections with the wider public.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
